# Local config. Note `.claude/*`, not `.claude/` — an ignored *directory* is never
# descended into, so the negations below would not take effect against `.claude/`.
# The two doctrine files are project knowledge and travel with the repo; everything
# else in here (settings, local state) stays local.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/GAME-DATA-PRINCIPLES.md
.env
nul

# Data
.impeccable/
# Note `streams/*`, not `streams/` — an ignored *directory* is never descended into,
# so the negations below would not fire against `streams/`. Same trap as `.claude/`.
#
# a6131eae09 blanket-ignored this directory. The three files added afterwards stayed
# tracked (ignore rules don't apply to tracked files), which is exactly what hid the
# problem: `streams/` looked fine in git while the two files nothing had re-added were
# invisible. HOMECOMING_PARSER.md — cited from ~17 files as `See HOMECOMING_PARSER` —
# survived only on one machine, and DEDUCTIVE_SCHEMA_HARNESS.md, cited from 11, was
# already gone from disk and had to be restored from a6131eae09^.
#
# These five are project record and travel with the repo. Scratch and per-session notes
# stay local by default.
streams/*
!streams/HOMECOMING_PARSER.md
!streams/DEDUCTIVE_SCHEMA_HARNESS.md
!streams/REARRANGEABLE_LAYOUT_PLAN.md
!streams/OPEN_ITEMS.md
!streams/CHANGELOG-DISCORD.md
!streams/BUILD_PREVIEW_IMAGE_PLAN.md
!streams/BUILD_PREVIEW_BACKFILL_PLAN.md
raw_data_homecoming-raw_data_homecoming-20251209_7415/
# exported_powers/ (repo root) is now COMMITTED — it's the converter input, so a fresh
# clone / CI can regenerate generated/ from it without the gitignored .pigg source.
# The exporter's raw output copy under tools/bin-crawler/exported_powers/ stays ignored
# (re-ignored further down). See the "commit the converter input" GOAL in HOMECOMING_PARSER.md.
exported_powers_BETA/
texture_library/
raw_data_homecoming-20251209_7415/
MidsReborn-master/
texture_library2/
# DSH5 harness transient cache (canonical export dump derived from the gitignored
# .mhd + parser export). The distilled baseline (oracle_divergence_rules.json) is
# committable; the raw intermediates are not.
tools/mids-oracle/.oracle_cache/
# Thunderspy Mids' Reborn DB reference drop (44MB binaries + icon dumps).
# Reference asset only — useful icons are already extracted into
# public/img/powers/ via scripts/attic/extract-thunderspy-icons.py. Not app data.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root, and it must stay that way. An unanchored
# `Thunderspy/` matches at any depth, and `core.ignorecase` is true on macOS
# and Windows checkouts — so it also swallowed `src/data/datasets/thunderspy/`.
# Files already tracked there kept working, which is what hid this: only NEW
# files under the Thunderspy dataset went silently un-added. That is how a
# Thunderspy-only fix ships as a no-op.
/Thunderspy/
Mids MXD files/
dump/
tools/ghidra-audit/project/
CoH-Planner.code-workspace
completed/
bins/

# Python bytecode caches (anywhere in the repo)
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Tool suite: commit source, ignore build artifacts and generated data
tools/pigg-wrangler-dist/build/
tools/pigg-wrangler-dist/dist/
tools/bin-crawler/exported_powers/
tools/bin-crawler/**/static/cache/

# Playwright MCP test artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Engine artifacts (src/engine/wasm/, src/engine/wasm-node/, public/engine/) are COMMITTED,
# deliberately. They are built by `npm run build:engine` from the private rebuild repo plus a
# Rust/wasm toolchain — none of which a GitHub-hosted runner has, and the rebuild being private
# means CI cannot even check it out without a secret. Committing them is what makes this repo
# self-sufficient: deploy and CI both need only Node. Refresh them with `npm run build:engine`
# and commit the result whenever the engine changes.

# Understand-Anything scratch: the tool moves superseded batch/graph JSON into a
# timestamped trash dir. 132 files of it were committed once, and it is the reason
# scripts/verify-sync.cjs scopes its wiring grep — an unscoped grep matched half of
# scripts/ inside tool scratch and was permanently red.
.ua/.trash-*/

# Debug scratch (probes, .bak snapshots, test-run logs). Individual probe
# scripts get force-added and tracked when a committed comment or doc cites
# them by path as census evidence — same convention as the canonical fork.
/.scratch/

# vitest-only flattened dataset bundles, rebuilt by globalSetup on every run
.dataset-bundles/
